                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>Why did HRX succeed where many celebrity brands fail?</h3>
                                        <p>Celebrity-category authenticity (Hrithik's genuine fitness commitment) + accessible pricing + Myntra distribution + long-term Hrithik involvement. Multiple factors align.</p>
                                        <h3>Should other celebrities build brands?</h3>
                                        <p>Only if authentic category match + long-term commitment + accessible positioning. Celebrity-mismatched + short-term-focused celebrity brands typically fail.</p>
                                        <h3>Can new athleisure brands compete with HRX?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes in category niching (women's athleisure specialty, yoga-specific, running-specific, specialty fitness). HRX dominates celebrity-fitness mainstream.</p>
                                        <h3>Is HRX successful post-2020 fitness surge?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes — pandemic fitness surge + continued Hrithik involvement + category expansion drove growth. Sustainable brand equity.</p>
